From 756d682b3a83224a45a6626ca0cacd37d07f4c2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:58:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Remote card-change memo: key the ledger by content,
 not object identity

The unloaded host pass (INTERVAL_S 30 s) keyed `_remote_change_pass`'s skip memo on the
`_remote_links(stale_ok=True)` card dicts by identity. A warm stale_ok read refreshes in the
background, and that refresh republishes a NEW projection whenever the entry is older than
`_LINKS_MAX_AGE_S` (15 s). So every steady-state pass saw new dicts for an unchanged ledger and the
memo never hit in production replica mode (fail-safe: a miss runs the full pass, but the claimed
skip never happened).

Fix: `_ledger_content_key` digests (blake2b, sorted rows) the ledger-card fields
`replica_cards` reads (owner labels, profile-board cards, cold-start fallback) and the pass keeps:
key, board, id, gateway, profile, session, origin_session, origin_gateway, origin_profile, status,
unfinished, released, ownership_state. The memo is compared by equality; no objects are held.

Why it shipped: the PR's tests monkeypatched `_remote_inputs_key` itself, so nothing exercised the
real `_remote_links` across >15 s gaps.

Tests (tests/tui_gateway/test_remote_card_outcomes.py): the real `_remote_inputs_key` over the real
`_remote_links`, clock +30 s per pass, refresh run inline, projector returning new dicts each call.
- unchanged content: projections republish, remote reads stay flat (memo hits) - RED on base
- key/status/session/origin_session/profile/gateway/released change: the pass runs
- mutant dropping "profile" from the key fields is caught.

Follow-up from review of #3349 (t_c0dda0fd22abf9d8); card t_bbea93e8bb9553ba.
